What was changed:
  - Rebranded from "hermes-agent" / "Hermes Agent" to "Kova Agent".
  - Renamed Python modules (hermes_cli -> kova_cli, hermes_platform ->
    kova_platform, hermes_state* -> kova_state*), npm packages
    (@hermes/* -> @kova/*), and the CLI entry points.
  - Replaced the user interface.
  - Removed the upstream contributor-email mapping directory
    (contributors/) and .mailmap, which map commit emails to GitHub
    logins for upstream's own release tooling. Those tools are not
    used by this fork.

What was NOT changed:
  - The license itself.
  - Upstream model identifiers (e.g. nousresearch/hermes-4-405b), which
    name real models served by third-party providers. Renaming them
    breaks model routing.
  - Third-party project names referenced in documentation.

